---
import ThreeMfConverter from '../components/converter/ThreeMfConverter';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../config/site';

const title = '3MF to STL Converter — Free, No Upload | IntoSTL';
const description = 'Convert 3MF files to STL directly in your browser while preserving final geometry and transforms. Free, private and no upload required.';
const questions = [
  {
    question: 'Are 3MF build transforms preserved in the STL?',
    answer: 'Yes. The validated conversion applies supported build-item transforms so the STL contains the final positioned geometry.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Will the converted STL keep colors and materials?',
    answer: 'No. STL stores surface geometry only, so colors, materials, textures and other 3MF metadata are not included.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does IntoSTL upload my 3MF file?',
    answer: 'No. The file is read and converted locally in your browser and is not sent to an IntoSTL server.',
  },
  {
    question: 'When is STL useful for compatibility?',
    answer: 'STL is useful when a slicer, viewer or older 3D-printing application expects surface geometry in STL format.',
  },
];
const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'IntoSTL 3MF to STL Converter',
    url: absoluteUrl('/3mf-to-stl/'),
    description,
    applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    isAccessibleForFree: true,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'IntoSTL', item: absoluteUrl('/') },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: '3MF to STL', item: absoluteUrl('/3mf-to-stl/') },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: questions.map(({ question, answer }) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer },
    })),
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/3mf-to-stl/" structuredData={structuredData}>
  <article class="tool-page">
    <header class="tool-intro shell-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free browser tool</p>
      <h1>Convert 3MF to STL</h1>
      <p>Turn the final geometry in a 3MF model into a binary STL without sending the file anywhere.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="shell converter-wrap">
      <p class="privacy-note"><span aria-hidden="true">●</span> Private by design. Your files are processed locally in your browser and are not uploaded to our servers.</p>
      <ThreeMfConverter client:load />
    </div>

    <nav class="on-this-page shell-narrow" aria-labelledby="three-mf-page-nav">
      <p id="three-mf-page-nav">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#three-mf-how">How to convert 3MF to STL</a></li>
        <li><a href="#three-mf-preserved">What is preserved</a></li>
        <li><a href="#three-mf-lost">What is lost</a></li>
        <li><a href="#three-mf-why">Why convert</a></li>
        <li><a href="#three-mf-faq">FAQ</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="shell-narrow content-stack">
      <section aria-labelledby="three-mf-how">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 id="three-mf-how">How to convert 3MF to STL</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Use the 3MF to STL converter when you need the model's final surface geometry in a simpler format. The file stays on your device throughout the conversion.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Upload a 3MF file</strong><p>Choose a model up to 50 MB from your device.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Inspect the geometry</strong><p>IntoSTL combines the model's build items and transforms, then shows the STL geometry in 3D.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Download the STL</strong><p>Save one binary STL containing the final transformed geometry.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="two-column" aria-labelledby="three-mf-preserved">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Conversion details</p>
          <h2 id="three-mf-preserved">What is preserved when converting 3MF to STL?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The validated conversion path preserves the final mesh geometry. Multiple build items are included, and their supported transforms are applied to the output vertices so their final positions are represented in the STL.</p>
          <p>The preview shows this combined, transformed geometry before download. The binary STL then stores the resulting triangles as one geometry file.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="two-column" aria-labelledby="three-mf-lost">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Format limits</p>
          <h2 id="three-mf-lost">What 3MF data STL cannot keep</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>STL stores surface triangles, so it cannot preserve 3MF colors, materials, textures or document metadata. These details are omitted rather than approximated or reconstructed.</p>
          <p>If those richer properties matter to the next stage of your workflow, keep the original 3MF alongside the converted STL.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="two-column" aria-labelledby="three-mf-why">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Compatibility</p>
          <h2 id="three-mf-why">Why convert 3MF to STL?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>3MF can store richer printing information, while STL is a simpler geometry format supported by a broad range of slicers, viewers and older workflows. That can be useful when the next application accepts STL but not 3MF.</p>
          <p>Current slicer workflows such as OrcaSlicer, PrusaSlicer and Bambu Studio can work with modern formats, but a particular exchange step or older tool may still require STL. Convert only when surface geometry is what the destination needs.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="three-mf-faq">
        <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p>
        <h2 id="three-mf-faq">3MF to STL FAQ</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {questions.map(({ question, answer }) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{question}</summary>
              <p>{answer}</p>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="related-tool">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Related tool</p><p class="related-heading">Starting from an STL?</p></div>
        <a class="secondary-button" href="/stl-to-3mf/">Convert STL to 3MF</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
